{"resourceIdentifier":"2414","resourceName":"Davidson County Landfill","description":"The Davidson County Landfill is a municipal solid waste facility operated by Davidson County in Lexington, North Carolina. During the project period covered by this report, landfill gas was collected and routed for combustion at one of two devices: a single open flare or an electricity generator set. Both devices were operated by Davidson Gas Producers using landfill gas collected at the Davidson County Landfill. Since the commissioning of the electricity generator set in November 2010, the flare only operated as a backup methane destruction device. The landfill gas collection system consisted of 56 vertical wells. Eleven wells were located at the older, closed Holly Grove area of the landfill, thirty-nine were in Phase 1 area of the landfill, and six wells in Phase 2 area of the landfill. There is a total of eleven wells connected to the leachate cleanout system for a total of 67 wells. The landfill does not re-circulate leachate back into the landfill and is not considered a Bioreactor as defined by U.S. EPA.","location":{"latitude":35.836708,"longitude":-80.173958},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2021-04-07","endExclusive":"2021-05-08","endInclusive":"2021-05-07"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"2414"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"NC"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ANEW ENVIRONMENTAL, LLC"},{"type":"string","value":"Texas, United States"},{"type":"string","value":"(281) 207-7217"},{"type":"string","value":"mhavel@anewclimate.com"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"2414"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"50000"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CA